==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|dividende||lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|dividendum||lang=la|thing to be divided}}, future passive participle of {{term|divido||lang=la|to divide}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{arithmetic}} A number or [[expression]] that is to be divided by another.
#: ''In "42 ÷ 3" the '''dividend''' is the 42.''
# {{finance}} A [[pro rata]] payment of money by a [[company]] to its [[shareholder]]s, usually made periodically (eg, [[quarterly]] or [[annually]]).

====Hyponyms====
* {{sense|finance: pro rata payment}} [[regular dividend]], [[special dividend]]

